WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.780
In this video, we are going to take a look
at the career of one of the most surprising

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.320
and controversial figures of the Century.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.820
That figure is Mikheil Saakashvili.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:32.620
Wait a second, don’t you know him?

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:38.130
Well, imagine a person who is capable of being
the one of the best of allies of Washington

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:42.120
and, at the same, the greatest enemy of Vladimir
Putin.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.410
He was &nbsp;the president of one country, a candidate
to preside over another, and, today, he doesn´t

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:48.430
even have a nationality.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:53.280
A man, a politician worthy of starring in
a political thriller.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:01:00.730
In fact, now that I mention it, it wouldn't
be surprising to see a Netflix original produced

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:01.730
about this guy..

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:17.829
Well, this is today´s character: Mikheil
Saakashvili.

00:01:17.829 --> 00:01:22.479
MISHA, THE GOVERNOR

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:26.319
In order to start our story, we need to go
back to May the 30th, 2015.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:32.119
That day, Petro Poroshenko, the president
of Ukraine, appointed Mikheil Saakashvili

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:36.210
as the governor of the province of Odessa.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.950
With this position, Misha was given Ukranian
nationality.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:43.880
However, to become a Ukranian citizen, &nbsp;he
had to give up citizenship from his home country,

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:51.500
Georgia: a country he had led as President
between 2004 and 2013.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.329
His addition to the Ukrainian government was
quite the treat for the media.

00:01:55.329 --> 00:01:56.859
And it is only logical.

00:01:56.859 --> 00:02:01.399
You see, at that time, Ukraine was going through
a really tense situation.

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:05.430
After the so-called Maidan revolution and
the fall of the pro-Russian president, Victor

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:09.760
Yanukovich, there was almost a feeling of
civil war in Ukraine: a war between Kiev´s

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.300
supporters, and Moscow´s.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.920
And Odessa was one of the most pro-Russian
provinces.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.920
So you can imagine the whole picture: a foreign
ex president, and not just any ex president,

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.700
but one of Putin´s worst enemies, appointed
as governor of Odessa...

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:28.000
This event was hugely discussed in all the
national as well as international press.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.450
The president of Ukraine who was, by the way,
an old friend and fellow college student of

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:38.100
Misha´s, Petro Poroshenko, described Misha
as “the man w upho makes possible the impossible”

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.100
Flattering...right.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.140
At that time their friendship seemed to be
“bulletproof”.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:47.280
Well, the mission of the new governor was
to stabilize Odessa, grant power to Kiev,

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:54.120
chase corruption, and set the groundwork for
the region to prosper.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.870
In order to carry it all out, Misha brought
many of his former collaborators from Georgia.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:02.910
He also hired many Ukrainian young professionals
who he thought to be corruption free, like

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:07.970
Yulia Marushevska, an activist who became
famous here on YouTube, with the video “I

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.420
am a Ukrainian”.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:14.530
Misha also brought in some people from Putin´s
opposition in Russia, like the Russian activist

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:18.600
Maria Gaidar, who was appointed Vice-Governor,
no less.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:30.560
There was a lot to do and it had to be done
fast so… as it was said, so it was done.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.490
Once he took the Odessa governorship, the
new governor started a thorough investigation

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:37.390
to find and punish corrupt public workers.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:41.240
He changed most of the high level positions
in the Public Administration; He simplified

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:46.310
the process to create companies, and introduced
independent controls and even liberated public

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:50.710
beaches that had been illegally occupied,
so that once again Odessa’s citizens could

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:51.710
enjoy them.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:57.430
And hold on a second here, because Misha has
a strange work methodology: it is as effective

00:03:57.430 --> 00:03:58.850
as it is controversial.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:04.890
If anything doesn't work properly and is corrupt,
he dismantles it, fires all the workers and

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:05.890
sets it up again.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:09.760
He did the same during his time in office
in Georgia with the Traffic Police, and he

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:14.070
threatened to do it again with the Odessa
Port, the largest commercial port in Ukraine,

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:17.100
well-known for the bribes and payments to
the customs officers.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.000
“We need to fire them all.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.139
We have 130 new people.

00:04:20.139 --> 00:04:23.750
They are young, new and trained, and the old
ones are hopeless”.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.130
- Mikheil Saakashvili.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:29.370
In the end, he only had to fire some of the
customs officers so the corruption would stop.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:30.370
Look:

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:34.680
“A number of businessmen noted that bribes
at the port really had stopped in recent months,

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:38.900
mainly because people were scared of becoming
the next victim of one of Saakashvili’s

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.490
public anti-corruption tirades”.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:43.290
- Shaun Walker, correspondent of The Guardian.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:48.120
With all these changes and with the help of
Misha's contacts, Odessa started to receive

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.380
help from the USA.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:53.520
And, since Misha didn't trust the Police,
the first thing he did was establish an independent

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.730
police force to fight corruption.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:03.420
A police force that was organized and trained
by the FBI and the California Highway Police!

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:06.750
So, it looks like everything was going fine,
right?

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:11.990
Then just wait, because both Saakashvili and
his team soon realized it was all going to

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:15.190
be much harder than they anticipated...

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:19.940
The problem was that Odessa was not a battle
field of Kiev´s supporters vs Pro-Russians…

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:24.180
but it was a battlefield between the rule
of law and an oligarchy that has dominated

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:29.870
Ukraine since its independence.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:35.780
THE KINGDOM OF OLIGARCHS

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:44.180
More and more experts have said so: Ukraine´s
biggest problem is not Russia, it is the oligarchy.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:48.430
Corruption in Ukraine is so embedded that
we could almost say it is a sort of feudal

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:55.950
country where the nobility are, of course,
the almighty oligarchs.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:00.860
They control the companies, the political
power, the administration, the media...

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:06.260
Almost nothing escapes their power, consolidated
by money and fear.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:10.850
Their level of impunity is almost absolute:
police, government and judges are part of

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:11.850
the game.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.940
Things have been this way since Ukraine got
its independence.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:19.510
But, since the Maidan Revolution, it all got
much worse.

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:23.900
After the fall of the Pro-Russian president
Viktor Yanukovich and with the civil conflict

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:28.680
the country was going through, the new government
felt incapable of trusting the army or the

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.040
police since both institutions were corrupt,
disorganized and badly-equipped.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:37.889
That is why he made a decision: he appointed
several oligarchs as governors of some of

00:06:37.889 --> 00:06:40.430
the most vulnerable regions in the country.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:44.860
These oligarchs paid for their own private
armies, and with nice incentives, the police

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.880
followed their orders as well, earning a sum
for the head of every separatist.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.320
Yes, just as I told you.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:53.880
The government placed the mafia directly in
charge of several governorships.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:07:03.050
That was the case for Ihor Kolomoisky, who
was appointed governor of Dnipropetrovsk,

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:05.820
one of the most important provinces of the
country, economically speaking.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:10.270
Yes, this is the Ukraine Mikheil Saakashvili
was dealing with.

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:14.600
“There is not a single state enterprise
in Ukraine that has not been usurped by one

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.040
clan or another”.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.949
Aivaras Abromavicius, former minister for
economy and trade of Ukraine

00:07:19.949 --> 00:07:25.150
As you can imagine, all these oligarchs did
not welcome Misha or his reform agenda.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:29.250
Once, he was even kicked out of an interview
when he suggested all of these mafia members

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:30.729
had to be sent to prison.

00:07:30.729 --> 00:07:34.080
Remember, the media is also the property of
the oligarchy...

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:41.330
The thing is Misha soon started to work to
fight, and end, this situation.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:47.960
“I will do whatever it takes for complete
victory to rid Ukraine of this filth, of this

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:52.450
corrupt scum, which capitalize on the blood
of our soldiers […] whose only motivation

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:57.560
in life is to fill its own pockets, strengthen
its own clan and bleed Ukraine dry”.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:59.169
Mikheil Saakashvili

00:07:59.169 --> 00:08:00.300
And so he did.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:04.759
Misha started to publicly report all kinds
of influence peddling, favourable treatment

00:08:04.759 --> 00:08:05.759
and privileges.

00:08:05.759 --> 00:08:10.240
On one occasion, he came on national television
and reported the details of a corrupt scheme

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:15.220
of the airlines owned by Kolomoisky, an oligarch
who nearly obtained a monopoly on national

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.220
flights.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:19.930
The public report ended the situation and
took many of the people involved to court...but

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:23.340
as you can imagine...Mr. Kolomoisky didn´t
take it well...

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:27.360
He promised to get revenge and here’s what
he said about Saakashvili, in public:

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:32.460
“When a dog without a muzzle bites someone,
we need to punish both the dog and, more importantly,

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:33.460
its owner”.

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:34.460
Ihor Kolomoisky

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:42.640
Now, do not think all Misha did was to report
the oligarchs… not at all.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:47.010
THE TRAIN CRASH

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:50.040
Saakashvili's reforms in Odessa didn't completely
work.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:53.600
Many of them were stopped and sabotaged by
the government in Kiev...

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:57.520
This wasn't just the oligarchs...you see,
corruption was so commonplace that it was

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:04.810
difficult to tell the difference between the
mafia and the authorities...

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.120
Misha didn't think twice.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.440
The government also became his target.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:14.140
Many analysts claim that this new war against
the government had a hidden agenda: to take

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:15.870
a leap to national politics.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:16.870
Well, maybe…

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:18.460
And the thing is, he did it.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:22.460
He started by reporting the corruption of
the very Prime Minister, Arseniy Yatsenyuk,

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:27.260
and many ministers followed... even his own
friend, the president Petro Poroshenko, the

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:29.550
person who had placed him in Odessa.

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:34.070
“What difference for Ukrainians does it
make who will treat them like dirt: Poroshenko

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:37.260
or Yanukovych; what difference who will steal
from them?”

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.360
Mikheil Saakashvili

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:39.840
The friendship didn't last long.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:44.330
As we have seen, Poroshenko appointed Misha
governor in May 2015.

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:48.150
In just a year the battle had begun.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:54.190
Finally, in November 2016, Misha resigned
as governor and began his own political party:

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:55.860
the MNF.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:58.550
And he soon gained more than 20,000 members.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:02.520
Yes, the former Georgian president now wanted
to lead Ukraine.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:07.310
In his own words, he aspired to turn this
disaster of a country into a complete European

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:08.779
superpower.

00:10:08.779 --> 00:10:16.610
But you might be wondering about the response
of Poroshenko and the government to this campaign...

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:18.330
Pay attention:

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:24.300
In July 2017 Poroshenko took advantage of
the fact that Misha was in the USA and revoked

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:25.940
his Ukrainian citizenship.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:29.380
All of a sudden, Mikheil Saakashvili was a
stateless person.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:33.240
Now, if you think that stopped him...you are
very wrong.

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:36.470
Look, when his nationality was taken away,
Misha moved to Poland.

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:40.290
And we have to say Misha is well-loved in
Eastern Europe.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:46.620
In fact, many countries offered him citizenship...but
no, Misha was determined to go back to Ukraine.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.500
And that is exactly what he did.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.660
Despite the warnings of the government in
Kiev, on September 10th, surrounded by a supportive

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:56.980
crowd, Misha crossed the border on foot between
Poland and Ukraine.

00:10:56.980 --> 00:11:10.380
The images of his confrontation with the border
guards are… quite a sight.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:22.430
By the way, what do you think he’s up to
now that he’s back?

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:26.380
Despite his irregular situation...Misha is
campaigning around the country..

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:27.380
All of that said…

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:35.910
there is still an unanswered question: Why
Mikheil Saakashvili?

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:40.230
THE SAAKASHVILI REVOLUTION

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:44.820
In 2003, Misha lead a popular uprising against
the corrupt Georgian political system of Eduard

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:45.820
Shevardnadze.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:49.580
And, in what was known as the Rose Revolution,
he even made it to the Georgian parliament.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:53.649
Elections were held and as the successful
revolution’s leader, Saakashvili easily

00:11:53.649 --> 00:11:56.070
beat the rest.

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:57.540
The reform process started.

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:02.350
A fierce fight against corruption and a tough
policy towards Moscow that became a model

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:05.000
for the former soviet countries.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:10.459
But we will discuss these matters as well
as the dark and less glamorous side of Saakashvili

00:12:10.459 --> 00:12:12.820
in a future video, here at VisualPolitik.

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:17.550
For now, it is your turn: Do you think Misha
will end up leading Ukraine?

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:21.160
Leave your answer in the comments as well
as in this survey.

